Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: require an exact PCI address for VFCT VBIOS

The first VFCT entry with matching vendor/device/slot/function IDs
currently wins even if its PCI bus differs. Two RX 7900 XTX boards with
different subsystem IDs consequently load the same VBIOS. On rivers-host
this changes
the second board from three DP ports and one HDMI port to two of each,
and its Xiaomi display disappears.

Restore strict PCI address matching. When bus renumbering prevents an exact
match, fall back to the driver's other BIOS retrieval methods instead of
using a different board's image. This changes the driver's selection only;
it does not flash either GPU's ROM.

Based on Linux 7.2.6. Reassess when upgrading the kernel.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_bios.c
@@ -377,13 +377,10 @@
  * @adev: AMDGPU device
  * @vhdr: VFCT image header to check
  *
- * VFCT entries contain the PCI bus number as recorded during BIOS POST.
- * On systems where the kernel renumbers PCI buses (e.g. pci=realloc or
- * resource conflicts), the runtime bus number may differ from the POST
- * value.  Match by device identity (vendor + device + function) and use
- * the bus number as a preference: exact bus match is preferred, but when
- * the bus numbers disagree we accept the entry if the device identity
- * matches.
+ * GPUs with the same vendor and device IDs can have different board BIOSes.
+ * Require an exact PCI address match to avoid selecting another GPU's image.
+ * If PCI buses were renumbered, let the other BIOS retrieval methods run
+ * instead of accepting an ambiguous VFCT entry.
  *
  * Returns: 0 on match, -ENODEV on no match
  */
@@ -395,19 +392,11 @@
 	    vhdr->DeviceID != adev->pdev->device)
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	if (vhdr->PCIDevice != PCI_SLOT(adev->pdev->devfn) ||
+	if (vhdr->PCIBus != adev->pdev->bus->number ||
+	    vhdr->PCIDevice != PCI_SLOT(adev->pdev->devfn) ||
 	    vhdr->PCIFunction != PCI_FUNC(adev->pdev->devfn))
 		return -ENODEV;
 
-	/* Exact bus number match - preferred */
-	if (vhdr->PCIBus == adev->pdev->bus->number)
-		return 0;
-
-	/* Bus mismatch but device identity matches (PCI renumbering case) */
-	dev_notice(adev->dev,
-		   "VFCT bus number mismatch: table %u != runtime %u, matching by device identity (vendor 0x%04x device 0x%04x)\n",
-		   vhdr->PCIBus, adev->pdev->bus->number,
-		   adev->pdev->vendor, adev->pdev->device);
 	return 0;
 }
 
